{"text":"I've done three searches and can't find the specific library you're remembering. The closest thing that surfaced is Meta's own [Hardware Art package](https://developers.meta.com/horizon/downloads/package/oculus-controller-art/) (official SVG/lineart assets, not a React library) and a community [quest-controls-mapper](https://github.com/AniketMan/quest-controls-mapper) project — neither is an npm component library.

Do you recall anything else about it — the package name, where you saw it, or what it rendered? That would help me track it down.

Otherwise I'm happy to keep going with the custom `QuestController` component I already built — it covers all the buttons with press and hold states and is already wired into the app.","textMode":"visible_message"}
